# Arno IPTables Firewall: rsyslog configuration
#
# This template configures rsyslog to capture and isolate firewall messages
# generated by the 'arno-iptables-firewall' service. It ensures that logs
# starting with the 'AIF:' prefix or tagged with 'firewall:' are written
# to a dedicated log file without being processed by other rules.

# Service name used in log messages and as process identifier.
# Default: arno-iptables-firewall
set $service_name = {{ NAME | default('arno-iptables-firewall') }};

# Enable verbose output (1 to enable, 0 to disable).
# While this variable is primarily for the script itself, we document
# its intent here for completeness in the configuration context.
# Default: 0
# Note: rsyslog does not use the VERBOSE flag directly; this comment
# serves as documentation for the package parameters.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Section 1: Log and stop messages containing the 'AIF:' prefix
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Match kernel facility messages that contain the string 'AIF:'
# (Arno's IPTables Firewall). These are asynchronous (-) and then
# discarded (& stop) to prevent duplicate logging.
if $syslogfacility-text == 'kern' \
and $msg contains 'AIF:' then -/var/log/arno-iptables-firewall
& stop

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Section 2: Log messages with the 'firewall:' tag
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Match messages explicitly tagged with 'firewall:'.
# These are written asynchronously to the same dedicated log file.
if $syslogtag == 'firewall:' then -/var/log/arno-iptables-firewall
